 - Dosage forms MUST be strictly compatible:\n26:      - Tablets/Capsules (اقراص, كبسول, حبوب, فيلم, شريط) ONLY match Tablets/Capsules.\n27:      - Syrups/Suspensions (شراب, شرب, معلق) ONLY match Syrups. NEVER match tablets with syrup.\n28:      - Creams (كريم) ONLY match Creams. NEVER match cream with ointment or suppository.\n29:      - Ointments (مرهم, دهان) ONLY match Ointments.\n30:      - Injections/Ampoules (امبول, حقن, فيال) ONLY match Injections.\n31:      - Suppositories (لبوس) ONLY match Suppositories.\n32:      - Drops (نقط, قطرة) ONLY match Drops.\n33:      - Sprays (بخاخ, سبراي) ONLY match Sprays.\n34:    - COMBINATION PRODUCTS (Zero Tolerance): Commercial suffixes like \"كو\" (Co), \"كومب\" (Comp), \"بلس\" (Plus) denote a multi-ingredient combination product (e.g. adding a diuretic or second active agent). A combination product (e.g. \"دواء كو\" / \"Drug Co\") MUST NEVER match a single-ingredient plain product (\"دواء\" / \"Drug\"). Return \"no_match\".\n35:    - If dosage forms or combination types conflict, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n36: \n37: 3. STRENGTH / CONCENTRATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR MISMATCH):\n38:    - If the requested drug specifies a strength (e.g. 457mg, 600mg, 500mg, 1000mg/1gm, 20mg, 40mg) and the candidate has a DIFFERENT numeric strength:\n39:      YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n40:    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\n41:      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\n42:      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\n43:      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. \"ربع\" equals 0.25mg / 250mcg).\n44: \n45: 4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & WHOLESALE UNITS (MATCH vs REVIEW):\n46:    - \"match\": Same brand, same form, same strength.\n47:      - STANDARD PACKS: If requested shortage specifies standard packaging count (e.g. 20 tablets, 5 ampoules, 3 strips) and warehouse candidate has the same drug, form, and strength but does not explicitly state the pack size (e.g. standard listing without count):\n48:        THIS IS 